🔍 Detailed Breakdown: Decentralized Freelance Marketplace
🧩 Project Overview

A decentralized alternative to Upwork or Fiverr — where freelancers and clients interact directly, and blockchain handles escrow, payments, and dispute resolution.

⚙️ Blockchain (Smart Contract Features)

Tech: Solidity on Ethereum / Polygon
Smart Contracts to build:

User Registration Contract – Registers wallet addresses as freelancers or clients.

Job Posting Contract – Allows clients to create job offers stored on-chain with description hashes (stored on IPFS).

Escrow Contract – Manages locked funds for each job:

Client deposits funds in escrow.

When freelancer marks job as done, client approves → funds released automatically.

Optional arbitration function for disputes.

Reputation Contract – Stores ratings and completion stats per user.

🧠 Backend (Node.js + Express + Database)

Responsibilities:

User Management (JWT or OAuth + wallet linking)

Off-chain Data: Store job metadata, chat messages, user profiles, and reputation stats.

IPFS Integration: Upload job descriptions, deliverables, or portfolio files.

Event Listener: Listen to blockchain events (e.g., JobCreated, PaymentReleased) and update database in real time.

API Endpoints:

/api/jobs → CRUD for jobs

/api/users → manage profile info

/api/escrow/:jobId/release → trigger payment

💻 Frontend (React / Next.js)

UI Components:

Landing Page: Browse freelancers or jobs.

Dashboard:

Freelancers: track proposals, active jobs, funds earned.

Clients: create new jobs, release escrow payments.

Wallet Connection: MetaMask integration to interact with contracts.

Job Detail Page:

Displays job description, budget, and escrow status.

“Apply Now” or “Release Payment” buttons (depending on role).

Chat & Notifications: Real-time updates from backend.

Profile Page: Shows reputation, completed jobs, linked wallet.

